    Submit
  </button>
</form>
```

### Modals & Dialogs

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Full screen on mobile, centered on desktop
<div className="fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-end sm:items-center justify-center">
  <div className="bg-white w-full sm:w-auto sm:max-w-lg sm:rounded-lg max-h-screen overflow-y-auto">
    <div className="p-4 sm:p-6">
      Modal content
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

## Touch & Interaction

### Touch Targets

**Minimum touch target size: 44x44px (Apple HIG) or 48x48px (Material Design)**

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Adequate touch target
<button className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] p-2">
  <Icon className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>

// ❌ Bad - Too small for touch
<button className="p-1">
  <Icon className="w-4 h-4" />
</button>
```

### Interactive Element Spacing

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Sufficient spacing between touch targets
<div className="flex gap-2 sm:gap-3">
  <button className="px-4 py-2">Button 1</button>
  <button className="px-4 py-2">Button 2</button>
</div>

// ❌ Bad - Too close together on mobile
<div className="flex gap-1">
  <button className="px-2 py-1">Button 1</button>
  <button className="px-2 py-1">Button 2</button>
</div>
```

## Text & Content

### Readability

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Readable line length
<article className="max-w-full sm:max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4">
  <p className="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
    Content text with good readability
  </p>
</article>

// ❌ Bad - Too wide on desktop, too narrow on mobile
<article className="w-full">
  <p className="text-sm">
    Content text
  </p>
</article>
```

### Text Truncation

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Handle long text gracefully
<p className="truncate sm:whitespace-normal">
  Long text that might overflow on mobile
</p>

// Use break-words for URLs or long strings
<p className="break-all sm:break-words">
  https://very-long-url.example.com/path/to/resource
</p>
```

## Testing Requirements

### Manual Testing Checklist

Before marking a component as complete, test on:

- [ ] Mobile (< 640px) - iPhone SE, Android small phones
- [ ] Tablet (768px - 1024px) - iPad, Android tablets
- [ ] Desktop (> 1024px) - Standard laptop/desktop screens
- [ ] Large desktop (> 1440px) - Large monitors

### Browser DevTools

Use browser responsive mode:

1. Chrome DevTools: `Cmd/Ctrl + Shift + M`
2. Test common devices:
   - iPhone SE (375px)
   - iPhone 12/13/14 (390px)
   - iPad (768px)
   - Desktop (1280px, 1920px)

### Touch Testing

If possible, test on actual mobile devices to verify:
- Touch targets are easy to tap
- Gestures work correctly (swipe, pinch-zoom where applicable)
- Forms are easy to fill on mobile keyboards
- No horizontal scrolling (unless intentional)

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### 1. Fixed Widths

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Fixed pixel widths break on different screens
<div className="w-[800px]">Content</div>

// ✅ Good - Relative widths or max-width
<div className="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto">Content</div>
```

### 2. Desktop-Only Features

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Hover-only interactions (mobile has no hover)
<div className="opacity-0 hover:opacity-100">
  Important content
</div>

// ✅ Good - Touch-friendly alternatives
<button onClick={toggleContent} className="md:hidden">
  Show Details
</button>
<div className="hidden md:block md:opacity-0 md:hover:opacity-100">
  Content visible on click (mobile) or hover (desktop)
</div>
```

### 3. Overflow Issues

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Can cause horizontal scroll on mobile
<div className="flex gap-6 p-8">
  <div className="min-w-[300px]">Wide content</div>
  <div className="min-w-[300px]">Wide content</div>
</div>

// ✅ Good - Responsive with proper overflow handling
<div className="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 p-4 sm:p-8">
  <div className="w-full sm:w-auto">Content</div>
  <div className="w-full sm:w-auto">Content</div>
</div>
```

### 4. Tiny Text on Mobile

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Too small to read on mobile
<p className="text-xs">Important information</p>

// ✅ Good - Readable on all devices
<p className="text-sm sm:text-base">Important information</p>
```

## Performance Considerations

### Images

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Responsive images with srcset
<img
  src="/image-800w.jpg"
  srcSet="/image-400w.jpg 400w, /image-800w.jpg 800w, /image-1200w.jpg 1200w"
  sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px"
  alt="Description"
  className="w-full h-auto"
/>

// ✅ Good - Use Next.js Image component
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src="/image.jpg"
  alt="Description"
  width={800}
  height={600}
  className="w-full h-auto"
  sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 800px"
/>
```

### Lazy Loading

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Lazy load below-the-fold content
<div className="space-y-4">
  {items.slice(0, 5).map(item => <ItemCard key={item.id} {...item} />)}
  
  <div ref={loadMoreRef}>
    {isInView && items.slice(5).map(item => <ItemCard key={item.id} {...item} />)}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Accessibility + Responsive

Responsive design must maintain accessibility:

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Accessible on all screen sizes
<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
  <button 
    className="md:hidden"
    aria-expanded={isMenuOpen}
    aria-controls="mobile-menu"
  >
    Menu
  </button>
  
  <div 
    id="mobile-menu"
    className={`${isMenuOpen ? 'block' : 'hidden'} md:block`}
  >
    <a href="/home" className="block py-2 md:inline-block md:py-0">
      Home
    </a>
  </div>
</nav>
```

## Documentation

When creating new components, document responsive behavior:

```tsx
/**
 * UserCard Component
 * 
 * Displays user information in a card format.
 * 
 * Responsive behavior:
 * - Mobile: Stacked layout with avatar on top
 * - Tablet+: Horizontal layout with avatar on left
 * - Actions always full width on mobile, auto on tablet+
 * 
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <UserCard user={userData} />
 * ```
 */
export function UserCard({ user }: UserCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

## Summary Checklist

For every UI component, ensure:

- ✅ Mobile-first approach (default styles for mobile, then `sm:`, `md:`, etc.)
- ✅ Touch targets ≥ 44x44px
- ✅ No horizontal scrolling on mobile
- ✅ Text is readable (min 14-16px on mobile)
- ✅ Buttons/actions are accessible on small screens
- ✅ Forms are easy to use on mobile keyboards
- ✅ Tables either scroll horizontally or transform to cards
- ✅ Images are responsive and properly sized
- ✅ Spacing appropriate for screen size
- ✅ Tested on actual devices or browser DevTools
- ✅ No hover-only interactions without touch alternatives

## Enforcement

The AI assistant should:
- **Always** apply responsive classes when creating new components
- **Warn** when detecting fixed widths or desktop-only patterns
- **Suggest** mobile-first alternatives when reviewing code
- **Test** mentally through different breakpoints before suggesting code
- **Refuse** to create non-responsive UI without explicit user override

This is a **mandatory** requirement, not optional. Mobile users are first-class citizens.
