  sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, (max-width: 1024px) 50vw, 800px"
  alt="Description"
  className="w-full h-auto"
/>

// ✅ Good - Use Next.js Image component
import Image from 'next/image';

<Image
  src="/image.jpg"
  alt="Description"
  width={800}
  height={600}
  className="w-full h-auto"
  sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 800px"
/>
```

### Lazy Loading

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Lazy load below-the-fold content
<div className="space-y-4">
  {items.slice(0, 5).map(item => <ItemCard key={item.id} {...item} />)}
  
  <div ref={loadMoreRef}>
    {isInView && items.slice(5).map(item => <ItemCard key={item.id} {...item} />)}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Accessibility + Responsive

Responsive design must maintain accessibility:

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Accessible on all screen sizes
<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
  <button 
    className="md:hidden"
    aria-expanded={isMenuOpen}
    aria-controls="mobile-menu"
  >
    Menu
  </button>
  
  <div 
    id="mobile-menu"
    className={`${isMenuOpen ? 'block' : 'hidden'} md:block`}
  >
    <a href="/home" className="block py-2 md:inline-block md:py-0">
      Home
    </a>
  </div>
</nav>
```

## Documentation

When creating new components, document responsive behavior:

```tsx
/**
 * UserCard Component
 * 
 * Displays user information in a card format.
 * 
 * Responsive behavior:
 * - Mobile: Stacked layout with avatar on top
 * - Tablet+: Horizontal layout with avatar on left
 * - Actions always full width on mobile, auto on tablet+
 * 
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <UserCard user={userData} />
 * ```
 */
export function UserCard({ user }: UserCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

## Summary Checklist

For every UI component, ensure:

- ✅ Mobile-first approach (default styles for mobile, then `sm:`, `md:`, etc.)
- ✅ Touch targets ≥ 44x44px
- ✅ No horizontal scrolling on mobile
- ✅ Text is readable (min 14-16px on mobile)
- ✅ Buttons/actions are accessible on small screens
- ✅ Forms are easy to use on mobile keyboards
- ✅ Tables either scroll horizontally or transform to cards
- ✅ Images are responsive and properly sized
- ✅ Spacing appropriate for screen size
- ✅ Tested on actual devices or browser DevTools
- ✅ No hover-only interactions without touch alternatives

## Enforcement

The AI assistant should:
- **Always** apply responsive classes when creating new components
- **Warn** when detecting fixed widths or desktop-only patterns
- **Suggest** mobile-first alternatives when reviewing code
- **Test** mentally through different breakpoints before suggesting code
- **Refuse** to create non-responsive UI without explicit user override

This is a **mandatory** requirement, not optional. Mobile users are first-class citizens.
